      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "rates"
        ],
        "note": "57,567 rows over TWO pollutant-processes: 57,040 for 9101 across 23 operating modes and 527 for 11710 across seventeen (400-416). THE TWO MODE FAMILIES ARE DISJOINT AND THAT IS NOT A COINCIDENCE THIS DOCUMENT RELIES ON: tire wear's modes are binned on average speed alone and are produced by a different generator (see `pp_W`), so a rate row of one pollutant-process is contracted only against its own family's weights. Of the seventeen, mode 400 -- `tirewear;idle` -- carries meanBaseRate exactly 0.0 in all 31 of its rows and is never reached at Inventory scale either (docs/process-tirewear.md 3.2). Read whole, keyed six ways by J22.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
