        "note": "3 rows: 9101 (Total Energy x Running Exhaust), 10710 (PM10 Tirewear, chained) and 11710 (PM2.5 Tirewear x Tirewear). This relation is the fixture's SECOND output-block axis and the only place the run's pollutant/process scope is written down -- it comes from here and never from the RunSpec XML. It is also what `pp_W` is keyed by: the PROCESS half of each id decides which of the two operating-mode generators wrote its weights.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
